2\t\n     3\tThis document is the operator-facing reference for every environmen
t variable\n     4\tconsumed by the production backend binaries that serve Custo
mer / Agent / CI\n     5\ttraffic through the Yalla Control Plane API. Postgres 
source of truth owns all\n     6\ttenant data; the Provisioning worker talks to 
Dokploy, which is the private\n     7\tprovisioning engine:\n     8\t\n     9\t-
`/usr/local/bin/yalla-api`\n    10\t- `/usr/local/bin/yalla-worker`\n    11\t\n 
  12\tConfiguration is resolved once at process startup from environment variabl
es\n    13\tlayered over per-profile defaults. The precedence chain is environme
nt variable\n    14\t> profile default. Environment variables are the production
default for backend\n    15\tprocesses.\n    16\t\n    17\tThe checked-in exampl
e at `deploy/config/control-plane.env.example` is the\n    18\tcanonical startin
g point. Operators install it as `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`\n    19\twith ow
ner `root:yalla` and mode `0640`, then replace every `<redacted:...>`\n    20\tp
laceholder from their secret manager.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Profiles\n    23\t\n
   24\t`YALLA_PROFILE` selects the deployment environment:\n    25\t\n    26\t| 
Profile | Strict | Typical use |\n    27\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    28\t| `local`
| No | Developer machine |\n    29\t| `test` | No | Unit and integration tests |
\n    30\t| `staging` | Yes | Pre-production validation |\n    31\t| `production
` | Yes | Live traffic |\n    32\t\n    33\tStrict profiles (`staging`, `product
ion`) fail fast when an operational field\n    34\tis missing. Local and test pr
ofiles supply permissive defaults so the backend\n    35\tstarts without real cr
edentials.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Required environment variables\n    38\t\n    3
9\t### `YALLA_PROFILE`\n    40\t- **Default:** `local`\n    41\t- **Allowed valu
es:** `local`, `test`, `staging`, `production`\n    42\t- **Description:** Selec
ts the configuration profile. An unrecognised value\n    43\t  causes the proces
s to exit immediately with a stable `E_CONFIG` error.\n    44\t\n    45\t### `YA
LLA_API_ADDR`\n    46\t- **Default:** `:8080` (local/staging/production), `127.0
.0.1:0` (test)\n    47\t- **Format:** `host:port`\n    48\t- **Description:** Th
e address the HTTP API listens on. The API binary does not\n    49\t  terminate 
TLS itself; TLS is terminated at the operator\'s reverse proxy.\n    50\t\n    5
1\t### `YALLA_PUBLIC_URL`\n    52\t- **Default:** `http://localhost:8080` (local
), `http://127.0.0.1` (test)\n    53\t- **Required for:** `staging`, `production
`\n    54\t- **Format:** Absolute `http` or `https` URL with a host\n    55\t- *
*Description:** The externally reachable base URL of the API. Used to build\n   
56\t  absolute links in responses and notifications.\n    57\t\n    58\t### `YAL
