verification tool is missing locally, `scripts/verify.sh` reports\n   147\tit ex
plicitly. The repository\'s policy is **never silently skip a\n   148\tcheck** —
an absent tool must either be installed or noted in\n   149\t`ralph/progress.txt
` so the gap is visible.\n   150\t\n   151\t## Dependency Review Expectations\n 
 152\t\n   153\tYalla pulls only what it needs. When you add or update a third-p
arty\n   154\tGo module, follow the checklist in\n   155\t[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](./
CONTRIBUTING.md#dependency-review-checklist) and\n   156\texpect the dependency-
review CI job to gate the PR. New modules with\n   157\tunknown licenses or know
n high-severity advisories will be rejected\n   158\tautomatically.\n   159\t\n 
 160\t## Container Image Hardening\n   161\t\n   162\tThe production `Dockerfile
` ships the `yalla-api` binary and\n   163\t`Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla
-worker` binary inside a\n   164\t`gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` ru
ntime so a leaked or\n   165\tcompromised image carries no shell, no package man
ager, no busybox,\n   166\tand no setuid binaries — only the service binary and 
the system CA\n   167\tbundle. The hardening posture is part of the public contr
act and is\n   168\tpinned by `internal/release/container_hardening_static_test.
go`; a\n   169\tregression in any one of the following is caught at build time:\
n   170\t\n   171\t- **Multi-stage build.** The Go toolchain, module cache, and 
source\n   172\t  tree never reach the runtime layer. A single-stage Dockerfile 
is\n   173\t  rejected.\n   174\t- **Distroless `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime
stage\'s base image\n   175\t  is pinned to `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:n
onroot` (UID/GID\n   176\t  65532). Debian/Ubuntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejec
ted because\n   177\t  they reintroduce a shell and a package manager.\n   178\t
- **`USER nonroot:nonroot`.** The runtime stage MUST run as the\n   179\t  non-r
oot user. A missing or partial (`USER nonroot`) directive is\n   180\t  rejected
.\n   181\t- **Hardened build flags.** The builder stage MUST invoke\n   182\t  
`go build` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` (static binary compatible with\n   183\t  the di
stroless static image), `-trimpath` (strip local filesystem\n   184\t  paths fro
m the binary), and `-ldflags="-s -w"` (drop the symbol\n   185\t  and DWARF tabl
es). Each missing flag is a separate regression.\n   186\t- **No `ADD <url>`.** 
Fetching arbitrary content at build time\n   187\t  without checksum verificatio
n is forbidden. Use `COPY` or a\n   188\t  `RUN curl ... | sha256sum -c` pattern
.\n   189\t- **No baked secrets.** The Dockerfile MUST NOT declare ENV values\n 
 190\t  whose key names contain `TOKEN`, `PASSWORD`, `SECRET`, `API_KEY`,\n   19
1\t  `PRIVATE_KEY`, `SIGNING_KEY`, or `DSN`. Secrets are supplied by\n   192\t  
the operator at runtime through environment variables, never\n   193\t  baked in
to the image.\n   194\t- **No package install in the runtime stage.** `apt-get`,
\n   195\t  `apt install`, `yum install`, `dnf install`, `microdnf install`,\n  
196\t  and `apk add` are rejected in the final layer. The builder stage\n   197\
t  is free to install build dependencies; the runtime stage is not.\n   198\t- *
*`COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:nonroot`.** Every\n   199\t  cross-stage C
OPY into the runtime layer MUST chown to the\n   200\t  non-root user so the cop
ied artefact is not owned by root.\n',
